# iOS minimum OS and latest SDK

User decision, 2026-11-10: Wawona builds with Xcode 27 and SDK 27 only. Xcode
27 accepts iOS deployment targets from **15.0**, so every iOS/iPadOS app
(App Store, TestFlight, Sileo `.deb`, TrollStore `.tipa`, simulator) targets
15.0. iOS 13 and 14 are no longer supported. Supersedes the 13.0 policy.

## Build contract

- `project.xcproj` sets `IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET = 15.0`; Nix products
 inherit it, no flake override.
- `xcode-prebuild.sh` `ld -r` takes `IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET`. Never hardcode.
- L0 `wwn-toolchain` still builds dependency archives at 13.0. Older minimums
 link into a 15.0 app; never link one newer than 15.0, never rewrite
 `LC_BUILD_VERSION`.
- tvOS, watchOS, visionOS and macOS keep their own targets.
- Never downgrade the SDK.

ObjC: CMake `CMAKE_OBJC_FLAGS` / Meson `objc_args` need the same
`-miphoneos-version-min` as C, or clang emits `_objc_release_xN` (iOS 16+)
and dyld aborts on iOS 15. Check
`wwn-toolchain/.github/scripts/verify-apple-objc-deployment.py`.

## Renderer and UI

One static ANGLE/Metal, one static MoltenVK/Metal. Metal policy in Rust.
SwiftUI APIs newer than iOS 15 need guards or `WawonaBackport`.

## Channels

All iOS binaries target 15.0; `cargo xtask artifact ios` requires it on
tipa and Sileo. Mode A firewall unchanged (no Cranelift, `MAP_JIT`,
Hypervisor, private Metal/IOMFB, QEMU). A deployment target does not extend
TrollStore's installer window or the iOS Hypervisor window. Store IPAs ship
no product `.dylib`. Never link GhosttyKit (iOS 17).

Compile, device operation, ASC processing and review are separate gates.

Reference: `Wawona/docs/agent-rules/wawona-ios-min-os.md`.
